# <%= formatName(name) %> - Next.js app

This is a web app built with Next.js.

## Tasks overview

You can run tasks for this project with:

```sh
npx nx <task-name> <%= directory %>
```

To view the list of available tasks, run:

```sh
npx nx show project <%= directory %> --web
```

The following tasks are included by default:

- `dev` – Start the local development server.
- `build` – Create a production build.
- `start` – Create and start a production build.
- `lint` – Check the source code with `eslint`.

## Development

To run this application locally, follow these steps:

```sh
# 1. Install dependencies in the root of the repository
npm install

# 2. Start the local development server
npx nx dev <%= directory %>
```

## Tests

```sh
npx playwright install chromium
npx nx test <%= directory %>
<% if (withMantine) { -%>
npx nx test <%= directory %>/shared/ui/ui-kit
<% } -%>
npx nx e2e <%= directory.replace(/\//g, '-') %>-e2e

# Update baselines locally, then review the changed PNGs
<% if (withMantine) { -%>
npx nx test <%= directory %>/shared/ui/ui-kit --skip-nx-cache -- --update
<% } -%>
npx nx e2e <%= directory.replace(/\//g, '-') %>-e2e --skip-nx-cache -- --update-snapshots
```

<% if (withMantine) { -%>
Vitest stores UI-kit baselines in `tests/__screenshots__/` in the UI-kit project.
Use the generated `expectScreenshot` helper when adding UI-kit screenshot tests.
<% } else { -%>
There is no UI-kit screenshot suite because this app was generated without the Mantine UI kit.
<% } -%>
Playwright stores page baselines beside their tests in `<spec>-snapshots/`.
The first local run creates missing baselines; later runs compare them without rewriting them.
Make baselines only on your local machine — never in Docker and never in CI: rendering depends on the OS, fonts, and Chromium version, and CI fails on a missing baseline instead of creating it.

E2E builds and runs the production app locally. Set `BASE_URL` in the environment to test a deployed app instead and skip both the local build and server.
